Terms of use – Real Dissections 3D (RD3D)
Hasselt University

1. Ownership
The RD3D platform, including 3D models, annotations and documentation, is the exclusive property of UHasselt.

2. Mandatory acknowledgement
In any use, UHasselt must be clearly acknowledged as owner of the platform.

3. Citation in publications
Any publication, presentation, thesis, teaching material or online communication based on the platform must explicitly mention UHasselt as developer.
Minimum wording
“These results were obtained using the RD3D platform, developed by UHasselt.”
Recommended citation – APA
UHasselt. (year of use). Real Dissections 3D (RD3D) – digital platform. Hasselt University. https://www.aquaticbiodiversityteam.be/education/RD3D.
Recommended citation – Chicago
UHasselt. Real Dissections 3D (RD3D) – digital platform. Hasselt University, accessed [date], https://www.aquaticbiodiversityteam.be/education/RD3D.

4. No transfer of rights
Free access does not grant any (intellectual property) rights to the platform or its content.

5. Permitted use
The platform may only be used for all non-commercial purposes. Modifications to content or functionality are prohibited without written consent from UHasselt.

6. Commercial use
Any direct or indirect commercial use is prohibited without prior written consent from UHasselt. UHasselt may require a license agreement and fee.

7. Disclaimer of liability
UHasselt cannot be held liable for any damage, errors, omissions or consequences resulting from the use of the platform, nor for decisions based on it.

8. Availability
UHasselt may take the platform offline, restrict or modify it at any time without prior notice. No right to continuity or compensation can be derived from this.

9. Privacy
Personal data of users will be used solely for access management, monitoring of use and communication about the platform, in accordance with UHasselt’s privacy policy.

10. Termination
In case of non-compliance with these terms, UHasselt may terminate access immediately.

11. Acceptance
By using the platform, the user declares to have read and accepted these terms.
